    "evidence": [
      {
        "id": "CE-77fd6c0246b391424e910734-span-7b76c6b811fdc3b4b7cd0dc4",
        "block_id": "b00029",
        "source_id": "report-06028a51c81cd54c4c83e008:main:af319a9993890019",
        "supporting_quote": "Overall, encorafenib plus binimetinib achieved an ORR of 58.3% (95% CI, 44.9-70.9), with three patients (5.0%) showing a CR and 32 (53.3%) showing a PR as their best response ( Figure 1 ). Responses were achieved after a median of 2.4 months (95% CI, 2.1-3.1) and lasted for a median DoR of 6.5 months (95% CI, 4.2-8.6). The ORR was 59.6% (95% CI, 45.1-73.0) and 50% (95% CI, 15.7-84.3) in patients treated with first- and second-line encorafenib plus binimetinib, respectively. The icORR was 46.7% (95% CI, 33.7-60.0), with 3 patients (5%) achieving an icCR. The median icDoR was 8.3 months (95% CI, 3.5-11.9) ( Supplementary Figure S1 )."
      },
      {
        "id": "CE-77fd6c0246b391424e910734-span-613e3fba4c357199c9b2da5d",
        "block_id": "b00018",
        "source_id": "report-06028a51c81cd54c4c83e008:main:af319a9993890019",
        "supporting_quote": "Demographic and disease attributes were collected to characterize the target population receiving encorafenib plus binimetinib. Efficacy endpoints comprised objective response rate (ORR), defined as the percentage of patients that achieve partial response (PR) or CR as their best responses per Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors (RECIST) v1.1; duration of response (DoR), defined as the time elapsed from the first determination of response (PR or CR) to the progression of the disease or death, whichever occurs first; disease control rate (DCR), defined as the percentage of patients with CR, PR, or stable disease (SD) as their best response; intracranial ORR (icORR), defined as the percentage of patients that achieve intracranial partial response (icPR) or intracranial complete response (icCR) and DoR of intracranial response (icDoR) using equivalent definition to DoR for intracranial response; progression-free survival (PFS), defined as the time elapsed from the date of first dose of encorafenib plus binimetinib to date of disease progression per RECIST v1.1 or death, whichever occurs first; intracranial PFS (icPFS), defined as time from the date of first dose of encorafenib plus binimetinib to date of intracranial disease progression per RECIST v1.1 or death, whichever occurs first; and overall survival (OS), defined as the time from the start of treatment until the date of death due to any cause. For time-dependent endpoints, patients who were lost to follow-up or had no events by the time of the analysis were censored at the date of the last alive contact. Safety was assessed based on the frequency and severity of adverse events (AEs). AEs were codified using the Medical Dictionary for Regulatory Activities (MedDRA), and their severity was categorized according to the Common Terminology Criteria for Adverse Events (CTCAE) v5.0. Treatment compliance was measured by the duration of encorafenib plus binimetinib treatment and the proportion of patients requiring dose interruptions, dose reductions, or permanent treatment discontinuation."
      }
    ]
